  "reply_markdown": "1. **Q1 — E1 is incomplete.** Preserve recovery records when either survivors or unverified descendants remain (finding #1). The documented survivor-only scope leaves precisely the uncertain process case unprotected after commit. Also, a readable start time plus an unavailable command line does not prove that a generic `node` process is unrelated (finding #2). An in-memory replay returned `Alive=false`; a non-Windows panel record then returned `Active=false`. Unreadable start times correctly block indefinitely until exit or informed operator intervention; that is deliberate fail-closed behavior.\n\n2. **Q2 — Normal folding is protected, but committing its accounting is not atomic.** Per-producer files avoid cross-producer append contention. The exclusive handle protects the legacy file against a simultaneous cooperating appender, which retries after deletion. However, files are deleted before the replacement `.last` is saved. A crash or write failure loses the folded accounting and can leave an obsolete subtraction baseline (finding #3). Replaying a baseline of 10 against one newly written line produced `Total=1, Count=0`. Clamping prevents negative output but conceals the undercount. This loses diagnostic counts, not queued telemetry events.\n\n3. **Q3 — Windows improves; Linux retains the collision.** Exact ticks distinguish different Windows start times. Non-Windows comparisons still accept different starts less than one second apart: mocked one-tick and half-second differences both returned `alive` (finding #4). Therefore F54-3 is not fully closed across platforms. Older markers retain the previous owner check and remain removable when that check establishes the owner is gone.\n\n4. **Q4 — The light-panel behavior is consistent with the stated exceptions.** In-memory checks passed for ordinary acceptance, context fallback, light purposes, `-PanelAll`, and required-light routing. Ordinarily the weighty sibling suppresses the light entry; a context-skipped sibling permits the stand-in. `-Require` and `-PanelAll` intentionally allow both. Label and plan limits constrain concurrency, not membership. Required-light routing recorded both picked positions and the required lineage. The existing member ledger retains the stand-in reason; `panel.routing` records eligibility and picks. The documented pre-size-selection limitation remains: an eligible but subsequently unpicked weighty sibling suppresses fallback. No additional seating defect found.\n\n5. **Q5 — The adapter-specific invariants are unchanged, but shared recovery matters to every engine.** The delta leaves Claude authentication, model proof, quota classification and plan grouping unchanged. Findings #1–#2 concern shared lifecycle protection. The new launch hooks remain test-mode gated, and E4 implements the described first-nonblank-line anchor. All 11 changed PowerShell files parsed without errors; `git diff --check` passed. I did not run filesystem-writing harnesses.\n\n6. **Q6 — HOLD.** Findings #1 and #2 block acceptance. Resolve or explicitly disposition the telemetry accounting and Linux identity limitations in findings #3–#4. Run the post-fix suite before tagging; the reported quiet panel pass does not establish a full-suite pass for the final candidate.\n\n## Requested checks\n\n- **RC1:** Working directory: repository root; permission: workspace-write; procedure: extend `harness-fixes28e` RECORD with two fixtures—zero survivors plus one unverified descendant, and a recorded generic-runtime descendant whose start becomes readable while command-line inspection fails—then run `powershell -NoProfile -File tests/run-all.ps1 -Only harness-fixes28e`. Require retained recovery records and no subsequent reviewer launch for findings #1–#2. Budget: two fixtures, 10 minutes execution.\n- **RC2:** Working directory: repository root; permission: workspace-write; procedure: in an isolated telemetry home, establish a nonzero seen baseline, inject failure between counter-file deletion and `.last` replacement, restart, and append one new counter line. Require recoverable folded accounting and a since-flush count of one for finding #3. Budget: one fault-injection case, 5 minutes execution.\n- **RC3:** Working directory: repository root; permission: workspace-write; command: `powershell -NoProfile -File tests/run-all.ps1`. Require every harness passing on the final candidate, with no unexplained timing or parent-death failures. Budget: one quiet-machine run, 45 minutes.",
